    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n1. **Governance test failure**: `APPROVAL_STATUSES` was being imported from `./index.js` but wasn't being re-exported. I added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` from the schema module.\n\n2. **Eval test failure**: The `toxicityMetric` function was incorrectly treating the references array (passed as the second parameter from `runEvaluations`) as custom banned terms. I removed the optional `bannedTerms` parameter so the function always uses the default banned terms list.\n\n## Test Results\n- **Test Files**: 8 passed (8)\n- **Tests**: 28 passed (28)\n\nAll public exports remain working as expected\u2014the constants are still available both as named exports and in the default export object.",
